    "insights": [
      "S4 additivity reduces to algebra over the parent determinant/GCD bridge: signed-area additivity is a ring identity, boundary additivity is B(T1)+B(T2)=B(Q)+2*diagGCD (double-counting the shared diagonal), and the interior identity follows by clearing /2 in Pick formula.",
      "The general gluing law I(Q)=I(T1)+I(T2)+(diagGCD-1) has a clean meaning: the correction counts diagonal-interior lattice points migrating from boundary to interior; primitive edge (diagGCD=1) gives exact additivity."
    ],
